            "heading": "Low-grade vs High-grade dysplasia",
            "points": [
              "Low-grade dysplasia: pencillate hyperchromatic nuclei confined to the basal half of cells, preserved polarity, extending to the surface epithelium without maturation",
              "High-grade dysplasia: marked nuclear pleomorphism, loss of polarity, full-thickness stratification, complex cribriform/back-to-back architecture and atypical mitoses",
